, particularly for the elderly population.", "ESQUIUS:Esquius is another reference for nutritional standards in Spain, specifically including elderly populations.", "X CONGRESO DE LA SOCIEDAD DE NUTRICIÓN Y DIETÉTICA DE GALICIA:The X Congress of the Society of Nutrition and Dietetics of Galicia held in La Coruña in May 2000 focused on nutritional assessment for bedridden patients.", "SOCIETY OF NUTRITION AND DIETETICS OF GALICIA:", "GERIATRIC NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT:Geriatric nutritional assessment focuses on evaluating the nutritional needs and status of elderly patients, ensuring they receive appropriate care.", "CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO:The \"CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO\" refers to a measurement utilized in nutritional assessment to evaluate muscle mass and overall nutritional status. This measurement is taken at the midpoint of the non-dominant arm, serving as an important indicator for assessing body composition.", "CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO:The \"CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO\" is a measurement used to assess the muscle mass of individuals, particularly in the context of nutritional evaluations. This measurement is significant as it can indicate changes in muscle mass, which may decrease in cases of malnutrition. Thus, the circumferential measurement of the arm serves as an important tool in evaluating an individual's nutritional status and overall health.", "PROTEÍNAS PLASMÁTICAS:\"PROTEÍNAS PLASMÁTICAS\" se refiere a las proteínas presentes en el plasma sanguíneo, cuya concentración es un indicador clave del estado del compartimento proteico visceral. Estas proteínas son fundamentales en la evaluación nutricional, ya que se miden durante las valoraciones nutricionales para determinar el estado nutricional de los pacientes.", "RBP:RBP, or retinol-binding protein, is a crucial protein that plays a significant role in the transport of vitamin A within the body. It binds to retinol, which is essential for nutritional assessment and overall health. RBP is characterized by its short half-life, indicating that it is rapidly metabolized in the body. This protein is vital for maintaining adequate levels of vitamin A, which is important for various physiological functions, including vision, immune response, and cellular communication."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}